{"black_box_warning":{"current_value":"No FDA boxed warning identified in selected current DailyMed label.","fda_source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/215904s011s013lbl.pdf"],"proposed_value":"No FDA boxed warning identified in current FDA prescribing information.","rationale":"The current FDA label has warnings/precautions but no boxed-warning section. The row's conclusion is supported, but DailyMed is not permissible for this field.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect"},"blocking_questions":[],"fact_checks":[{"current_value":"ganaxolone","field":"generic_name","proposed_value":"ganaxolone","rationale":"FDA label and FDA approval materials identify ganaxolone as the active ingredient for ZTALMY.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/215904s011s013lbl.pdf","https://www.fda.gov/drugs/drug-trials-snapshots/drug-trials-snapshots-ztalmy"]},{"current_value":"Ztalmy","field":"trade_names","proposed_value":"Ztalmy","rationale":"ZTALMY is the FDA-approved proprietary name for ganaxolone oral suspension.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/215904s011s013lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"","field":"alternate_generic_names","proposed_value":"","rationale":"No separate alternate generic name requiring a separate alias field was identified; chemical/development aliases fit better in pubmed_search_aliases.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/9067315/"]},{"current_value":"CCD1042","field":"pubmed_search_aliases","proposed_value":"CCD 1042; CCD-1042; CCD1042; GNX","rationale":"CCD 1042 is verified in PubMed; FDA pharmacology review/search metadata also uses GNX. Current value is not wrong, but it is missing common spacing/hyphenation and GNX aliases useful for PubMed searches.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/9067315/","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/nda/2022/215904Orig1s000PharmR.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Yes; Available in US; 2022","field":"available_in_us/filter_availability/year_fda_cleared","proposed_value":"Yes; Available in US; 2022","rationale":"FDA approved ZTALMY on March 18, 2022, and the current label states Initial U.S. Approval: 2022.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.fda.gov/drugs/drug-trials-snapshots/drug-trials-snapshots-ztalmy","https://www.fda.gov/drugs/novel-drug-approvals-fda/new-drug-therapy-approvals-2022","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/215904s011s013lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"CDKL5 deficiency disorder; Current neuroactive-steroid ASM for seizures associated with CDKL5 deficiency disorder.","field":"epilepsy_type/filter_epilepsy_type/status_or_notes","proposed_value":"CDKL5 deficiency disorder; Current neuroactive-steroid ASM for seizures associated with CDKL5 deficiency disorder.","rationale":"FDA indication is treatment of seizures associated with CDKL5 deficiency disorder in patients 2 years and older; FDA describes ZTALMY as a neuroactive steroid GABA-A receptor positive modulator.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/215904s011s013lbl.pdf","https://www.fda.gov/drugs/news-events-human-drugs/fda-approves-drug-treatment-seizures-associated-rare-disease-patients-two-years-age-and-older"]},{"current_value":"Oral suspension; Liquid","field":"formulations_available/filter_formulation","proposed_value":"Oral suspension; Liquid","rationale":"FDA label lists oral suspension 50 mg/mL.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/215904s011s013lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"1800 mg/day for >28 kg; lower max for lower weights","field":"maximum_approved_daily_dose","proposed_value":"1800 mg/day for >28 kg; 63 mg/kg/day for <=28 kg, not to exceed 1800 mg/day; lower maximums apply in severe hepatic impairment","rationale":"Current label lists maximum 600 mg TID/1800 mg daily for >28 kg and 21 mg/kg TID/63 mg/kg/day for <=28 kg, with separate lower severe-hepatic-impairment dosing. Current value is broadly correct but incomplete.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/215904s011s013lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Weight-based titration to maintenance; pivotal CDD target up to 1800 mg/day for >28 kg; CDD: weight-based TID dosing; adults/children >28 kg 1800 mg/day","field":"minimum_effective_dose/typical_doses_per_day","proposed_value":"No separate minimum effective dose established; FDA label uses weight-based TID titration to maintenance, up to 21 mg/kg TID (63 mg/kg/day) for <=28 kg or 600 mg TID (1800 mg/day) for >28 kg","rationale":"FDA label supports TID weight-based titration and maintenance dosing, but does not identify a distinct minimum effective dose.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/215904s011s013lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Precise therapeutic mechanism is unknown; anticonvulsant effects are thought to result from positive allosteric modulation of CNS GABA-A receptors.; Moderate; GABA","field":"mechanism_of_action/mechanism_confidence/filter_mechanism","proposed_value":"Precise therapeutic mechanism is unknown; anticonvulsant effects are thought to result from positive allosteric modulation of CNS GABA-A receptors.; Moderate; GABA","rationale":"This closely matches FDA label mechanism language; 'Moderate' confidence is consistent with the label's 'unknown but thought to result' wording.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/215904s011s013lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"FDA/DailyMed labeling","field":"mechanism_source","proposed_value":"FDA prescribing information (Drugs@FDA/accessdata)","rationale":"The mechanism is supported by FDA labeling, but the named source should not include DailyMed under the trusted-source policy for this audit.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"missing_source","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/215904s011s013lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"CYP3A4 substrate; not a major inducer/inhibitor","field":"enzyme_inducing_or_inhibiting/filter_enzyme_effect","proposed_value":"Metabolized by CYP3A4/5 and other CYP/UGT enzymes; UGT inhibitors may increase exposure and strong/moderate CYP3A4 inducers decrease exposure; not a clinically relevant CYP inhibitor or inducer","rationale":"Current value captures CYP3A4 involvement and lack of major CYP induction/inhibition, but current FDA label also names UGT metabolism and UGT inhibitor interaction.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/215904s011s013lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"~34 h; Liver; Liver/hepatic","field":"half_life_range/major_organ_for_metabolism/filter_metabolism","proposed_value":"~34 h; Liver; Liver/hepatic","rationale":"FDA label states ganaxolone terminal half-life is 34 hours, is metabolized by hepatic CYP/UGT enzymes, and has altered exposure in hepatic impairment.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/215904s011s013lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"No clinically meaningful QT effect established; No known meaningful QT effect","field":"qt_interval_effect/filter_qt_effect","proposed_value":"At therapeutic exposures, ZTALMY does not prolong QTc; QT effects at high clinical exposure scenarios have not been 