dian difference 27.1%; Sperling2017 ganaxolone 1500 mg/day reported mean percent change, not median: -17.6% vs 2.0%, differential 19.6%)","reason":"Sperling2017 reports mean percent change, not median percent change; annotate before relying on it in a median field.","requires_user_approval":true,"source_urls":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/36870093/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/35429480/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/28230252/"]},{"current_value":"Sullivan2023|37.5|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/36870093/|21; Knight2022|27.1|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/35429480/|100; Sperling2017|19.6|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/28230252/|147","field":"plot_diff_median_pct_change_maximum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"Sullivan2023|37.5|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/36870093/|21; Knight2022|27.1|https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/35429480/|100","reason":"Sperling2017 value is mean percent change and should not be plotted as median percent change unless the plot parser supports an explicit mean label.","requires_user_approval":true,"source_urls":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/36870093/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/35429480/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/28230252/"]},{"current_value":"CYP3A4 substrate; not a major inducer/inhibitor","field":"enzyme_inducing_or_inhibiting","proposed_value":"Metabolized by CYP3A4/5 and other CYP/UGT enzymes; UGT inhibitors may increase exposure and strong/moderate CYP3A4 inducers decrease exposure; not a clinically relevant CYP inhibitor or inducer","reason":"Current FDA label contains UGT interaction and broader metabolism language not captured in the row.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/215904s011s013lbl.pdf"]}],"rct_link_checks":[{"label":"Downs2024","pmid":"38959712","proposed_action":"Keep as an RCT report link, but do not use for seizure-efficacy outcome extraction.","rationale":"The article is a double-blind placebo-controlled randomized trial report/secondary analysis of non-seizure outcomes in CDD; local PubMed metadata marks Clinical Trial Phase III/RCT. It does not provide extractable seizure efficacy outcomes for the plotted seizure columns.","status":"verified","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/38959712/"},{"label":"Sullivan2023","pmid":"36870093","proposed_action":"Keep.","rationale":"PubMed verifies a randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled phase 2 trial of oral ganaxolone versus placebo in PCDH19-clustering epilepsy, with ganaxolone maximum daily dose 63 mg/kg/day or 1800 mg/day and NCT03865732.","status":"verified","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/36870093/"},{"label":"Knight2022","pmid":"35429480","proposed_action":"Keep; disregard the deterministic title-only warning.","rationale":"PubMed verifies a randomized, placebo-controlled phase 3 trial of adjunctive ganaxolone versus placebo for CDD-associated refractory epilepsy. The title and abstract support the drug, seizure context, phase, randomization, and placebo control.","status":"verified","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/35429480/"},{"label":"Sperling2017","pmid":"28230252","proposed_action":"Keep.","rationale":"PubMed verifies a randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled phase 2 study of ganaxolone 1500 mg/day as add-on therapy in adults with uncontrolled partial-onset seizures.","status":"verified","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/28230252/"}],"source_updates":[{"current_value":"FDA Ztalmy approval/snapshot pages; FDA/DailyMed labeling","field":"evidence_sources","proposed_value":"FDA Ztalmy approval/snapshot pages; FDA prescribing information (Drugs@FDA/accessdata); PubMed RCT abstracts/metadata; ClinicalTrials.gov records for trial design where needed","reason":"Replace DailyMed with FDA label source and name PubMed/ClinicalTrials.gov support for RCT and outcome fields.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.fda.gov/drugs/drug-trials-snapshots/drug-trials-snapshots-ztalmy","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/215904s011s013lbl.pdf","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/35429480/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/36870093/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/28230252/","https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT03572933"]},{"current_value":"FDA/DailyMed labeling","field":"mechanism_source","proposed_value":"FDA prescribing information (Drugs@FDA/accessdata)","reason":"Mechanism wording is supported by FDA label; DailyMed is not needed and is outside the requested trusted-source list.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/215904s011s013lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"FDA/DailyMed SPL; status=no_boxed_warning_in_selected_label; setid=d91612c4-b03a-4be4-a1ee-6a13e3b83d4e; published=Dec 01, 2025; title=ZTALMY (GANAXOLONE) SUSPENSION [IMMEDICA PHARMA US INC]; url=https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=d91612c4-b03a-4be4-a1ee-6a13e3b83d4e","field":"fda_black_box_warning_source","proposed_value":"FDA prescribing information (Drugs@FDA/accessdata); status=no_boxed_warning_identified_in_current_fda_label; NDA=215904; revised=10/2025; title=ZTALMY (ganaxolone) oral suspension; url=https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/215904s011s013lbl.pdf","reason":"Black-box warning verification must use FDA/openFDA/FDA label/Drugs@FDA sources, not DailyMed.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2025/215904s011s013lbl.pdf"]}],"summary":"Ganaxolone/ZTALMY core FDA facts are supported: US approval/availability, CDD indication, oral suspension, TID weight-based dosing, GABA-A mechanism, adverse reaction percentages, half-life, hepatic metabolism, QT statement, and no FDA boxed warning. Updates are needed to replace DailyMed-based source text with FDA label/accessdata sources, add missing PubMed search aliases, and correct/annotate the median percent-change outcome because Sperling2017 reports mean percent change rather than median percent change."}
